+# Claire Trading — technical-debt, efficiency and UI review (2026-11-11)
+
+Read-only review at commit `61229a2`. No project file, service or database
+row was changed. Four parallel reviewers read every file in `app/`, `web/`,
+`bin/`, `mcp/` and `systemd/` in full; I ran the tests and linter, walked
+every dashboard page at desktop and phone width, timed the endpoints, and
+re-checked the findings marked **[V]** against the code or the live
+database myself. Unmarked items are a reviewer's reading of the code that I
+did not re-check. The 2026-11-03 review covered security; this one does not
+repeat it.
+
+**Summary.** The safety design is sound and the 2026-11-03 fixes held, but
+the code has grown by re-implementing things per feature instead of sharing
+them, and that duplication has started to produce wrong numbers on screen
+and a few real bugs on the money path. Nothing is slow today; the
+efficiency problems are wasted LLM turns and oversized polled payloads, not
+response times. The UI's biggest gaps are that no page answers "what do I
+hold, what protects it, what is pending", totals mix SGD and USD, and paper
+versus live is easy to miss.
+
+One thing to know about this review itself: `tests/test_smoke.py` runs
+against the live services when they are up, so each of my three full test
+runs sent one real "status?" chat turn to Claire and one live quote request.
+
+---
+
+## Status at the end of 2026-11-11
+
+Most of sections 2, 5 and 6.1–6.2 was done the same day. This list is the
+honest state; the sections below are the review as written and still
+describe the code BEFORE these changes (line numbers have moved).
+
+**Done and live**
+
+- Bugs: B1, B2, B3, B4, B5, B7, B9, B10, B11, B12, B13, B14, B15, and all
+  five "smaller ones". B6 in part (the ledger check runs; see below).
+- Logging (§3.5), with credentials scrubbed from every line.
+- Dead code (§5): the two `bob-dashboard` scripts, four systemd units, the
+  `custodian`/`autonomous` CLIs, seven unused functions, unused page code.
+- One exchange registry (`app/exchanges.py` + `DESK` in `nav.js`); three
+  side tables moved into `schema.sql`; ten indexes (§4.3).
+- `dashboards.py` split, steps 1, 2 and 4 (usage report, level and account
+  helpers, one error tail): 3,547 → 3,170 lines.
+- UI: grouped menu, PAPER / LIVE ARMED indicator, approvals badge, "Today"
+  home view, in-page confirmations everywhere, Reject guard, phone
+  viewport and standards mode on every page, base link style, plan-only
+  warning, deep links, polls that pause in hidden tabs.
+- Tests: 745 → 842, the suite 95 s → 45 s, the live smoke test opt-in.
+
+**Not done**
+
+- B8: the chat refusal rate has not been re-measured on the new prompt.
+- B6, second half: nothing compares the book's positions with what Saxo
+  holds. It needs a new read-only Saxo call that has not been tested
+  against the SIM account.
+- NSE's 2027 holidays: only the fixed dates are in until its circular is
+  published (the maintainer warns from 15 December).
+- §3.1 shared services: one positions/valuation implementation,
+  `market.price_in`, one `SaxoClient`, one claire-api client, `states.py`,
+  `repo.tx()`, a structured run-origin column.
+- §3.2: the view methods and POST handlers are still inside
+  `create_server` (steps 3, 5, 6, 7). §3.4: no schema version number.
+- §3.6: env-var documentation, `langchain-openai`, crash recovery under
+  systemd, floats in `check_risk`.
+- §4.1–4.2: SDK timeouts and concurrency cap, a real multi-turn chat
+  session, merged analyst sessions, `fetch_page` content extraction, the
+  Twelve Data credit budget, per-order Saxo polling, slimmer `/api/runs`
+  and `/api/approvals` payloads, HTTP/1.1 + gzip + ETag, N+1 queries,
+  scheduler jobs off the tick.
+- §6: one trade ticket (item 4), editable protection (7), the Runs page
+  search and filters (11), one vocabulary (13), time formatting (14), a
+  shared stale/error pill (15), not wiping edits (16), approval-card
+  jargon (17), most of accessibility (18), Claire chat (19).
+- Kept on purpose: `mcp/` and the `mcp_servers` table, `repo.apply_split`,
+  the four non-Claude providers, the old backups under `var/`.
+
+**Seen in the first hour of real logs**
+
+- Twelve Data answers 429 often enough that FX regularly falls through to
+  Yahoo and then the ECB (§4.1 item 6: the budget counts calls, not
+  credits).
+- On the live Saxo page, "Unrealised P/L" looked far out of scale against
+  the account total. Not investigated.
+
